    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1051">

                <pb facs="1206" n="1094" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1094"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Winterle/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-02T15:00:00+08:00">October 2, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 2—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Department’s 6, September 30, 6 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d1051-f1"/> I
                    instructed Ballantine and Paxton by telegraph October 1, 4 p.m. to proceed
                    immediately to Peiping for consultation. Paxton is leaving Chefoo today.
                    Following telegram received last night from Paxton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 1, 8 p.m. Your October 1, 4 p.m. Japanese Consul now requests
                            only recognition of United States Navy participation and expression of
                            regrets by American Consul. I am satisfied that Navy was involved.
                            Unless otherwise instructed am proceeding to Peiping October 2, 6
                            a.m.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1051-f1" n="90" xml:id="d1051-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it authorized the proposal made in paragraph 3 of telegram No. 20,
                    September 29, 5 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
